    slug: "cloud-computing-definition",
    shortDescription: "Define the NIST model.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nCloud computing is the on-demand delivery of IT resources over the internet with pay-as-you-go pricing. Key characteristics: on-demand self-service, broad network access, resource pooling, rapid elasticity, and measured service.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can explain cloud computing? What are its key characteristics accurately and connect the definition to a practical consequence. A strong answer should also acknowledge the main limitation or boundary.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Cloud computing is the on-demand delivery of IT resources over the internet with pay-as-you-go pricing.\n2. Key characteristics: on-demand self-service, broad network access, resource pooling, rapid elasticity, and measured service.\n3. Separate the service’s responsibility from the responsibilities of adjacent services, then state the main availability, IAM, networking, or cost consideration when relevant..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would define it first, explain the part that actually changes the outcome, and use the example to show I understand it in practice.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in an AWS-hosted service, a request or workload can pass through the AWS component described by the answer, and the team can verify the resulting routing, storage, or compute behavior. Cloud computing is the on-demand delivery of IT resources over the internet with pay-as-you-go pricing.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn an AWS-hosted service, this affects how traffic, compute, storage, identity, or monitoring behaves. Cloud computing is the on-demand delivery of IT resources over the internet with pay-as-you-go pricing.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Confusing services that operate at different layers.\n- Omitting the request or data flow between services.\n- Ignoring IAM, networking, availability, or cost when those constraints affect the answer.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nSeparate the service’s responsibility from the surrounding architecture. Mention the key boundary or limitation instead of describing AWS as a collection of interchangeable services.",
